The fixes are in, and the two changed source files compile on their own. I haven't run the game, and the full build of `supertux2` is still running in the background, so I haven't confirmed it links yet. I'll report back when it finishes.

**What the recording shows:** both groups of released coins bounce on the basin floor without ever settling, they fall through the water at normal speed, and they vanish once Tux swims up out of view, so they're gone when he comes back.

**Fixes:**

1. **Second burst flies too far** (`src/object/coin_explode.cpp`): the list of starting speeds for a burst was shared between bursts and got multiplied in place each time. So the second block threw its coins about 100 times harder than the first. Each burst now works from an unchanged copy of the base speeds.
2. **Coins never stop bouncing** (`HeavyCoin::collision_solid`): a coin bounced again whenever it landed faster than 20. Every bounce sends it back up at 99, so it always came down fast enough to bounce again. Now it only bounces if it lands faster than 200; otherwise it stops and its sideways speed is zeroed so it doesn't slide.
3. **Coins disappear off-screen** (`HeavyCoin::update`): coins were deleted as soon as they dropped below the bottom of the camera view. Now they're only removed if they fall below the bottom of the level, so they wait for Tux to come back.
4. **No slowdown in water** (`HeavyCoin::update`): coins now count as in the water the moment any part of them touches a water

